)\",\"language_code\":\"pt-br\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/pt-br/library/bg/9/30/\"},{\"display_name\":\"Русский (Russian)\",\"language_code\":\"ru\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/ru/library/bg/9/30/\"},{\"display_name\":\"Slovenčina (Slovak)\",\"language_code\":\"sk\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/sk/library/bg/9/30/\"},{\"display_name\":\"Slovenščina (Slovenian)\",\"language_code\":\"sl\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/sl/library/bg/9/30/\"},{\"display_name\":\"Українська мова (Ukrainian)\",\"language_code\":\"uk\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/uk/library/bg/9/30/\"},{\"display_name\":\"isiZulu (Zulu)\",\"language_code\":\"zu\",\"enabled\":false,\"url_path\":\"/zu/\"}],\"breadcrumb\":[{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/\",\"title\":\"Library\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/\",\"title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/\",\"title\":\"Chapter Nine: The Most Confidential Knowledge\"}],\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/30/\",\"bb\":2457,\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"pager\":{\"previous\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/29/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 29\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]},\"next\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/31/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 31\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":2777,\"bb\":568237,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/30/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"अपि चेत्सुदुराचारो भजते मामनन्यभाक् ।
साधुरेव स मन्तव्य: सम्यग्व्यवसितो हि स: ॥ ३० ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2778,\"bb\":2458,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/30/b2458/\",\"body_value\":\"api cet su-durācāro
bhajate mām ananya-bhāk
sādhur eva sa mantavyaḥ
samyag vyavasito hi saḥ\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2779,\"bb\":2459,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/30/b2459/\",\"shadow_value\":\"api – even; cet – if; su-durācāraḥ – one committing the most abominable actions; bhajate – is engaged in devotional service; mām – unto Me; ananya-bhāk – without deviation; sādhuḥ – a saint; eva – certainly; saḥ – he; mantavyaḥ – is to be considered; samyak – completely; vyavasitaḥ – situated in determination; hi – certainly; saḥ – he.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"api\",\"translation\":\"even\"},{\"word\":\"cet\",\"translation\":\"if\"},{\"word\":\"su-durācāraḥ\",\"translation\":\"one committing the most abominable actions\"},{\"word\":\"bhajate\",\"translation\":\"is engaged in devotional service\"},{\"word\":\"mām\",\"translation\":\"unto Me\"},{\"word\":\"ananya-bhāk\",\"translation\":\"without deviation\"},{\"word\":\"sādhuḥ\",\"translation\":\"a saint\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"saḥ\",\"translation\":\"he\"},{\"word\":\"mantavyaḥ\",\"translation\":\"is to be considered\"},{\"word\":\"samyak\",\"translation\":\"completely\"},{\"word\":\"vyavasitaḥ\",\"translation\":\"situated in determination\"},{\"word\":\"hi\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"saḥ\",\"translation\":\"he\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2780,\"bb\":2460,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/30/b2460/\",\"body_value\":\"Even if one commits the most abominable action, if he is engaged in devotional service he is to be considered saintly because he is properly situated in his determination.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2781,\"bb\":2461,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/30/b2461/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2782,\"bb\":2462,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/30/b2462/\",\"body_value\":\"Therefore a person who is situated in Kṛṣṇa consciousness and is engaged with determination in the process of chanting Hare Kṛṣṇa, Hare Kṛṣṇa, Kṛṣṇa Kṛṣṇa, Hare Hare/ Hare Rāma, Hare Rāma, Rāma Rāma, Hare Hare should be considered to be in the transcendental position, even if by chance or accident he is found to have fallen. The words sādhur eva, “he is saintly,” are very emphatic. They are a warning to the nondevotees that because of an accidental falldown a devotee should not be derided; he should still be considered saintly even if he has accidentally fallen down. And the word mantavyaḥ is still more emphatic. If one does not follow this rule, and derides a devotee for his accidental falldown, then one is disobeying the order of the Supreme Lord. The only qualification of a devotee is to be unflinchingly and exclusively engaged in devotional service.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2783,\"bb\":2463,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/30/b2463/\",\"body_value\":\"In the Nṛsiṁha Purāṇa the following statement is given:\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2784,\"bb\":2464,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/30/b2464/\",\"body_value\":\"bhagavati ca harāv ananya-cetā
bhṛśa-malino ’pi virājate manuṣyaḥ
na hi śaśa-kaluṣa-cchabiḥ kadācit
timira-parābhavatām upaiti candraḥ\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2785,\"bb\":2465,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/30/b2465/\",\"body_value\":\"The meaning is that even if one fully engaged in the devotional service of the Lord is sometimes found engaged in abominable activities, these activities should be considered to be like the spots that resemble the mark of a rabbit on the moon. Such spots do not become an impediment to the diffusion of moonlight. Similarly, the accidental falldown of a devotee from the path of saintly character does not make him abominable.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2786,\"bb\":2466,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/9/30/b2466/\",\"body_value\":\"On the other hand, one should not misunderstand that a devotee in transcendental devotional service can act in all kinds of abominable ways; this verse only refers to an accident due to the strong power of material connections. Devotional service is more or less a declaration of war against the illusory energy. As long as one is not strong enough to fight the illusory energy, there may be accidental falldowns. But when one is strong enough, he is no longer subjected to such falldowns, as previously explained. No one should take advantage of this verse and commit nonsense and think that he is still a devotee. If he does not improve in his character by devotional service, then it is to be understood that he is not a high devotee.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 9.30\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 9.30\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/